check by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{2{x}^{5/2}}{5}+C) &= \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{2{x}^{5/2}}{5})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\ &= \\frac{2}{5}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{5/2})+0 \\\\ &= \\frac{2}{5}\\cdot \\frac{5}{2}{x}^{5/2-1} \\\\ &= {x}^{3/2}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186503887 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8e537889-fa35-53e7-a7d1-c9526c47ddf5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2{x}^{3/2}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503895}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8e537889-fa35-53e7-a7d1-c9526c47ddf5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2{x}^{3/2}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503895} :answer-field/id #uuid "8523cfe1-fc1d-5cc8-b3ac-92d3c8d89541" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503892}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5ebfc4c0-4a2d-5c2d-be2b-47c6ddfe06d1" :question/problem "Find the antiderivative of ${x}^{1/2}.$\n\nWork on $x>0$.\n\nThe antiderivative is {{field-1}} $+C$. Enter only the term before $+C$, with no additive constant." :question/worked-solution "We can apply the power rule with $n=\\frac{1}{2}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {x}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{{x}^{1/2+1}}{(\\frac{1}{2}+1)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3/2}}{(\\frac{3}{2})}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{2{x}^{3/2}}{3}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, let's check by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{2{x}^{3/2}}{3}+C) &= \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{2{x}^{3/2}}{3})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\ &= \\frac{2}{3}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{3/2})+0 \\\\ &= \\frac{2}{3}\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}{x}^{3/2-1} \\\\ &